2	//!
3	//! Models the four chip registers the imported `tmp101.lgo` demo
4	//! cares about:
5	//!   - `0x00` — Temperature (16-bit, read-only).
6	//!   - `0x01` — Configuration (8-bit, read/write).
7	//!   - `0x02` — T_LOW   (16-bit, read/write — stub: stored verbatim).
8	//!   - `0x03` — T_HIGH  (16-bit, read/write — stub: stored verbatim).
9	//!
10	//! The 12-bit temperature value is laid out in the upper 12 bits of
11	//! the 16-bit register (0.0625°C / LSB; bits[3:0] always zero). The
12	//! current resolution mode in the config register is honoured at read
13	//! time, so a guest that reconfigures resolution between reads sees
14	//! values quantized to the new step size.
15	
16	use crate::peripherals::i2c::device::{Ack, I2cDevice};
17	
18	/// Default 7-bit address for the COR24-TB layout.
